# Normalize line endings.
#
# Without this file, line endings are whatever each contributor's core.autocrlf
# happens to be. The checkout on Windows carries CRLF on disk while the index
# stores LF, so any tool reading the working tree with autocrlf unset — a Linux
# shell, a container, CI — sees every line of every file as modified. That made
# `git status` report 36 untouched files as changed and would have turned a
# frontend commit into a CRLF rewrite of the whole backend.
#
# LF in the index and LF in the working tree, everywhere. Shell scripts and
# Dockerfiles need it anyway: a CRLF shebang inside an image fails with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M".
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated protobuf stubs — keep them out of diff review.
*.pb.go linguist-generated=true
*_grpc.pb.go linguist-generated=true
